      "description": "The user is projected onto the top textual material 'you know why muslims hates pigs?' which uses the second-person pronoun 'you' to directly address the viewer, inviting them to engage with the false stereotype being presented. This creates an implicit 'you' projection where the user is positioned as the one who should know or be aware of the supposed reason for Muslim hatred of pigs, thereby making the viewer complicit in the meme's rhetorical framing.",
